.nh
.TH "GHPM" "1" "Nov 2026" "ghpm 0.2.0-dev" "ghpm manual"

.SH NAME
ghpm-completion-zsh - Generate the autocompletion script for zsh


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBghpm completion zsh [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate the autocompletion script for the zsh shell.

.PP
If shell completion is not already enabled in your environment you will need
to enable it.  You can execute the following once:

.EX
echo "autoload -U compinit; compinit" >> ~/.zshrc
.EE

.PP
To load completions in your current shell session:

.EX
source <(ghpm completion zsh)
.EE

.PP
To load completions for every new session, execute once:

.SS Linux:
.EX
ghpm completion zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_ghpm"
.EE

.SS macOS:
.EX
ghpm completion zsh > $(brew --prefix)/share/zsh/site-functions/_ghpm
.EE

.PP
You will need to start a new shell for this setup to take effect.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for zsh

.PP
\fB--no-descriptions\fP[=false]
	disable completion descriptions


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	config file (default ~/.config/ghpm/config.yaml)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine readable output (where supported)

.PP
\fB--no-cache\fP[=false]
	bypass the release metadata cache

.PP
\fB--proxy\fP=""
	HTTP(S) proxy URL, overrides config


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBghpm-completion(1)\fP
